claimed: okay-script-interpolation -- the "JSP but Scala+Markdown" step the operator asked for. A new ScalaScript.render(markdown, classpath): Result, separate from run (run stays untouched, for apps/effects like the storefront). render recognizes ${expr} in PROSE (outside ```scala fences, $${ escapes to a literal ${) as a Scala expression evaluated in the SAME document-order scope ```scala blocks already build, its .toString appended to the output; prose text and non-scala fences pass through verbatim; the whole document becomes one synthesized @main body reusing the existing compile+load+invoke+stdout-capture engine (the rendered document IS Result.stdout). Brace-depth- and quote-aware scanner for ${...} (handles nested braces and a nested s"${...}" inside the expr). Literal text is embedded as a raw triple-quoted Scala string with a safe escaped fallback when the text itself contains an unsafe quote run.
